Z||000000||Thecrewchief1||04-02-2001||05:44 PM||||I replaced the dist (my cost $140) and my Fiero came back to life. Checked the old one with  a omh meter and it read 800, GM calls for 800 to 1500. They said it was still good, but I replaced it any ways to make sure. I left the old cap, rotor, and coil on it to make sure it ran right and it does. The new dist came with a new module so I don't know if my Accel coil and module are still any good. I'm going to the shop now and play around with it to see. Will post results later tonight. I think the old dist shaft was out because it chewed up the inside of the new cap as well the old cap I had put on to test the system for my little 3 mile ride after I put the old module in and it fired up. When I took the old cap off to change the dist this morning, it was chewed up as well. I know the meeting is coming up soon and I'd like to attend. My E-mail is Thecrewchief@aol.com, so please E-mail me with details, Thanks Bill||||reg||1
